#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example shows a new options for  including suspension springs modeled in Simulink. (Libraries > Models > Models: Simulink).
#
#In this run, two S-Functions are used to tightly couple the Simulink spring forces with the VS Math Model. The calculations from Simulink fit within the appropriate stages (kinematics and dynamics) of the VS Math Model.
#
#Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the suspension compliance datasets to see the settings for externally defined suspension springs.
#
#Click on the blue link "External Springs" to see how the Simulink model is connected to CarSim, and how to define the import and export variables that allow CarSim and Simulink to communicate.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

